      "side": 1,
      "message": "Two interaction and lifecycle considerations here:\n1. Link clicks vs message expansion: `gr-message` listens for click events on the host to expand the message. Clicking a link in the collapsed message will open the link in a new tab and simultaneously trigger message expansion.\n2. Rendering performance: Previously, `gr-formatted-text` was instantiated only for expanded messages (`renderExpandedMessageContent`), while collapsed messages used a plain text node. Rendering `gr-formatted-text` for all collapsed messages means every message on the change will eagerly parse markdown, sanitize HTML, and mount subcomponents on initial load.",
      "isAi": true,
